WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.757
Let’s trace this calculation carefully.

00:00:02.757 --> 00:00:09.352
Sales is one thousand and costs are eight hundred, so profit is two hundred.

00:00:09.352 --> 00:00:12.192
Tax is five percent of profit.

00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:18.082
Five percent is zero point zero five, so the tax becomes ten dollars.

00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:23.708
Net profit is two hundred minus ten, which gives one hundred ninety dollars.

00:00:24.348 --> 00:00:28.720
Notice the dependency chain. Net profit depends on tax.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:33.570
Tax depends on profit. Profit depends on sales and costs.

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.510
That kind of chain is common in analytics.

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:42.881
Change the tax rate to ten percent, predict the new result, and then run the cell to check yourself.
